# Common Normalized Event Fields (B1)

All parsers and pipelines in Group B should output these field names (based on Elastic Common Schema, ECS). If a log type does not have a field, leave it empty.

## Rules
1. Use the official ECS name. Do not invent new names.
2. Only include fields that can be filled from our datasets.
3. Prefer fields that detections use (IP, user, program, URL, status code).
4. Always keep the original raw line in `event.original`.

## Fields

| Meaning | ECS field | Apache access log | Windows JSON (Sysmon) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Event time | `@timestamp` | timestamp | `EventTime` / `@timestamp` |
| Original raw line | `event.original` | whole line | whole line |
| Log type | `event.dataset` | `apache.access` | `windows.sysmon` |
| Event type ID | `event.code` | - | `EventID` |
| Computer name | `host.name` | - | `Hostname` |
| Source IP | `source.ip` | client IP | `SourceIp` |
| Source port | `source.port` | - | `SourcePort` |
| Destination IP | `destination.ip` | - | `DestinationIp` |
| Destination port | `destination.port` | - | `DestinationPort` |
| User | `user.name` | - | `User` |
| Program path | `process.executable` | - | `Image` |
| Process ID | `process.pid` | - | `ProcessId` |
| Web method | `http.request.method` | GET, PUT, ... | - |
| Web path | `url.path` | request path | - |
| Web status | `http.response.status_code` | 200, 404, ... | - |
| Bytes sent | `http.response.body.bytes` | size | - |
| Referrer | `http.request.referrer` | referrer | - |
| Client / browser | `user_agent.original` | user agent | - |

## Change process
Need a new field? Tell B1 (Noor) in the team chat or open an issue. B1 adds a row here after the team agrees.
